+# Circuitiny browser/Arduino port
+
+Upstream: https://github.com/mfranzon/circuitiny
+Commit: 008c5f815f506da863e06f4239361c87aa42c060
+License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Marco Franzon. See LICENSE.
+
+Viewer3D.tsx and project/{schema,component,pins}.ts were copied and adapted from upstream. Native 3D part selection, TransformControls, PinAnchor picking and Bezier net rendering are reused. Web-only glue implements the original viewer store/catalog contract and writes to Velxio's authoritative native store/history.
+
+Local modifications: Arduino UNO native pin geometry; mini breadboard/resistor bodies; hidden real breadboard contacts; native edit commands and atomic move history; pin dropdowns; physical-hole collision and direct rail/ground guards; real native ngspice LED state; no remote HDR environment; native undo/redo, autosave and .vlx export.
+
+This is not the original desktop app or its ESP32 execution backend. Electron IPC, upstream AI/agents, ESP-IDF build/flash, native ESP32 HAL simulation and ESP32-specific DRC are not enabled. The existing local isolated AVR compiler, AVR8js and ngspice execute the Arduino project. KiCad and original inference graphs are not modified by this editor.
+
+Current 3D scope: UNO R3, mini170 breadboard, unrotated resistors/LEDs. Unsupported parts are reported; use native 2D editing for the full circuit. The full application retains Velxio's AGPL-3.0 licensing.
